# Task 3 report — Changes date and primary card polish

## Scope

Changed only the Task 3 page styles/markup, shared screen date-button style, and App integration tests:

- `src/pages/ChangesPage.tsx`
- `src/pages/ChangesPage.module.css`
- `src/pages/Screen.module.css`
- `src/App.test.tsx`

## Implementation

- Added a deterministic four-week Korean date selector in the Changes header. It uses a button with `aria-expanded`, `aria-haspopup="listbox"`, and `aria-controls`; each option communicates its selected state with `aria-selected`.
- Reworked the first Changes card to show the approved title `Flutter를 선호하지 않습니다.`, omit its CHANGED/90일 관찰 meta row, retain exactly the first two evidence lines, and remove the page footnote.
- Added the black circular check approval button with the accessible name `이 변화가 맞음`. It calls `resolveChange(item.id, 'accept')` directly.
- Kept the existing diff modal path on the long rounded `변경 내용 보기` button and retained the existing modal approval behavior.
- Added responsive visual styling for the 14px Korean date control, popover, compact primary actions, white-on-black circular check, and rounded details button.

## TDD evidence

1. Added an integration test that selects `8월 3일 — 8월 9일` and accepts the primary card using `이 변화가 맞음`.
2. Updated the existing Changes disclosure test to assert the approved title.
3. Ran the focused App test before implementation: 2 failures, specifically the missing date-picker button and old card title.
4. Implemented the minimum page and style changes.
5. Re-ran the focused App test: 15/15 pass.

## Verification

- `npm test -- src/App.test.tsx` — 15/15 tests pass.
- `npm run build` — TypeScript build and Vite production build exit successfully.
- `git diff --check` — no whitespace errors reported for tracked changes.

## Self-review

- Confirmed the primary card never renders its `CHANGED` or `90일 관찰` meta row.
- Confirmed the title is exactly `Flutter를 선호하지 않습니다.` and only two evidence entries are rendered.
- Confirmed the date selection is deterministic, stateful, and exposed to assistive technology.
- Confirmed direct approval and the existing modal approval both retain the repository integration.

## Concerns

None within Task 3 scope.

